1. Nf3 d5 2. g3 c5 3. Bg2 Nc6 4. d4 Bg4 5. Ne5 Nxe5 6. dxe5 e6 7. c4 Ne7 8. O-O
Qd7 9. h3 Bf5 10. Qb3 Nc6 11. Na3 Nd4 12. Qd1 Rd8 13. b4 Nc6 14. g4 Bg6 15. b5
Nb4 16. cxd5 Nxd5 17. Qb3 Qc7 18. Nc4 Be7 19. f4 O-O 20. e4 Nb4 21. f5 Rd3 22.
Qb2 Rd4 23. Qb3 Rd3 24. Qb1 Rc3 25. Nd6 Bxd6 26. exd6 Qxd6 27. a3 Qd4+ 28. Kh2
Nd3 29. fxg6 Nxc1 30. gxh7+ Kxh7 31. Rxc1 Rd3 32. Rd1 c4 33. Qc1 Rd8 34. Rxd3
cxd3 35. a4 $4 ({"A disastrous oversight.} 35. Qd1 {followed by 36 Rb1 won
easily." (BCM)... but Stockfish thinks Black is still winning after} d2 36. Rb1
Kg8 37. Kh1 Qf2 38. Bf1 Rd4 39. Qe2 Qxe2 40. Bxe2 Rxe4 41. Bd1 Re1+ 42. Kg2 g5
{, etc.}) (35. Qe1 $1 {is a distinct improvement on BCM's suggestion of 35 Qd1
as, after} d2 {, White has} 36. Qh4+ Kg8 37. Rd1 {and White is better but it
is still not easy to win.}) 35... d2 36. Qd1 {and White resigned (bulletin).}
0-1

