1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 g5 {Brentano's Defence.} 4. d4 {The best move.} Nxd4
5. Nxd4 exd4 6. Qxd4 Qf6 7. e5 Qb6 $1 ({Much better than} 7... Qg6 8. Nc3 Be7
9. Nd5 Bd8 10. O-O c6 11. Bd3 {Odam-Herzog, corr 1937.}) 8. Qxb6 axb6 9. Bxg5
Ra5 10. Nc3 ({To} 10. a4 {Black replies, of course,} c6 11. Bd2 cxb5 12. Bxa5
bxa5 13. axb5 b6) 10... c6 11. Bd3 Rxe5+ 12. Be3 Bc5 13. Nd1 d5 {"and the game
was drawn after another 12 moves". Source: CHESS, March 1949, Vol.14/162, p152}
1/2-1/2

